<ContentLayout title="About TokenCalculator.dev" description="Why TokenCalculator.dev measures LLM tokens locally and labels estimates honestly." heading="About"><p><strong>TokenCalculator.dev</strong> is an independent browser-based utility for developers, prompt engineers, and teams checking prompt size, API input cost, and context fit before calling an LLM.</p><h2>Mission</h2><p>The calculator is maintained around three commitments: user content remains on the device, calculation methods are labeled honestly, and changing provider facts link back to public sources.</p><h2>Tokenizer methodology</h2><p>OpenAI-family text uses <a href="https://github.com/dqbd/tiktoken">js-tiktoken</a> with the model’s configured encoding. Claude, Gemini, and DeepSeek use deterministic calibrated estimates where equivalent offline browser tokenizers are not available. Every result identifies whether it is exact, based on a provider formula, or estimated.</p><h2>Open model data</h2><p>Pricing and context limits are refreshed from the open-source <a href="https://models.dev/">Models.dev</a> catalog. A bundled, versioned registry keeps the calculator available when that public catalog cannot be reached. Provider invoices and official documentation remain authoritative.</p><h2>Editorial responsibility</h2><p>Pricing corrections, methodology questions, and reproducible calculation issues can be sent to <a href="mailto:hello@tokencalculator.dev">hello@tokencalculator.dev</a>. Substantive changes are reviewed against provider documentation before publication.</p><p><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> August 22, 2026.</p></ContentLayout>
